    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1043">

                <pb facs="0990" n="732" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg732"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1432</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Postmaster General</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Burleson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 30, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 31</hi>.] </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your letter of the 26th instant, enclosing a copy of a letter from
                    Frank A. Page, Industrial Trust Building, Providence, Rhode Island, relative to
                    the importation by parcel post from Germany of articles of German origin.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d1043-f1"/>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0991" n="733" xml:id="pg733"/>
                <p>In reply, I have to inform you that the parcel-post service is in operation
                    between the United States and Germany, the parcel-post mails for and from
                    Germany being dispatched via Rotterdam.</p>
                <p>The Department has no reason to believe that parcel-post mails from Germany for
                    this country or from this country for Germany have been interfered with by any
                    intervening country.</p>
                <p>By direction of the Postmaster General.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. A. Fisher</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Second Assistant Postmaster General</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
